.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ckman-config 1  ckman 
.SH NAME
ckman\-config \- Read or change device configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBckman\-config\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read or change device configuration
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
ckman\-config\-nfc(1)
Turn NFC on or off
.TP
ckman\-config\-reset(1)
Reset the device to factory defaults, erasing all applets and PINs
.TP
ckman\-config\-info(1)
Show the current device configuration
.TP
ckman\-config\-led(1)
Turn the LED on or off (device configuration patch)
.TP
ckman\-config\-ndef\-read\-only(1)
Allow or forbid NDEF writes (device configuration patch)
.TP
ckman\-config\-webusb\-landing(1)
Enable or disable the WebUSB landing page (device configuration patch)
.TP
ckman\-config\-pass(1)
Manage the PASS touch\-to\-type slots
.TP
ckman\-config\-ndef(1)
Read or replace the NDEF message
.TP
ckman\-config\-keyboard(1)
Manage the keyboard (HID) emulation layout
.TP
ckman\-config\-sm2(1)
Show or change the CTAP SM2 configuration (3.0+; writes need 3.1)
.TP
ckman\-config\-admin\-pin(1)
Manage the device Admin PIN
.TP
ckman\-config\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
